     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically given as up to 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual per-dose limit. The risk is lactic acidosis, and it applies even with normal kidney function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), which is the maximum dose.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day).\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is really what you want, for example under a specific protocol, confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording the confirmation. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
